  '<strong>Blackmail and fraud:</strong> do not pay or reply. Save screenshots and links and report through the Ministry of Interior’s Kollona Amn service or Absher. In an emergency call 999.',
  '<strong>Legal context:</strong> the Anti-Cyber Crime Law covers offences such as unauthorised access and online blackmail, and the National Cybersecurity Authority publishes guidance for individuals.',
  '<strong>Creators and sellers:</strong> if you advertise with a Mawthooq licence from the General Commission for Audiovisual Media, or run a store listed on Maroof, keep those details with the account name and email. They help show the account belongs to a real business.',
